course: dictionary
lesson: 2051
title: Conquest: taking control by force
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A conquest is when one group takes control of a country, city or people, usually by force in a war. «After the conquests, the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely.» The words that come after conquests, lands and traders, give you the clue: the lands were taken in war.
explain: Conquest can also mean beating a very hard challenge. «The conquest of a mountain» means climbing it after great effort, so it is a great achievement, not a war. Ask yourself: is someone being forced, or is someone reaching a goal? That question tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The conquests were terrible for the cities that resisted.» If "taking control of cities by force" makes sense there, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Conquest» means taking control of a country, city or people by force, usually in a war.
fact: «A conquest» can also be a place or land that has been taken in this way.
fact: «Conquest» can mean beating a very hard challenge, like «the conquest of a mountain».
fact: The Norman Conquest of England is a famous event you may study in history lessons.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word, and they often give clues to its meaning.
exercise: «After the conquests, the Mongol lands were peaceful enough for traders to travel safely.» What does conquests mean here? | Holidays by the sea | Trading goods in a busy market | *Taking control of lands by force | Hunting wild animals in the forest
exercise: «The team's conquest of the mountain took a whole year of hard work.» What does conquest mean here? | *Beating a very hard challenge | A boring walk with no goal | Losing a game on purpose | Painting a picture of the mountain
exercise: Find and copy one word that means fought back against. | conquests | terrible | cities | *resisted
test: «The Mongol empire was destructive in its conquests, but afterwards it kept trade routes safe.» What are its conquests? | Times it built new schools | *Times it took control of lands by force | Times it won a prize for sport | Times it held a big party
test: Which phrase uses conquest to mean a great achievement? | *The conquest of a mountain | Losing a race by a mile | A quiet lunch at home | A broken umbrella in the rain
exam: In the phrase «the Norman Conquest of England», what was taken? | A river | *England | Space | A mountain
